data: {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":6,"result":{"content":[{"text":"{\"series\":[{\"product_id\":14100287,\"coordinate\":\"1.7.1.1.1.1.0.0.0.0\",\"vector_id\":2062815,\"context\":{\"citation\":\"Statistics Canada. Table 14-10-0287-01, Labour force characteristics, monthly, seasonally adjusted and trend-cycle. Vector v2062815. Released 2026-11-06.\",\"table_id\":\"14-10-0287-01\",\"table_title\":\"Labour force characteristics, monthly, seasonally adjusted and trend-cycle\",\"table_url\":\"https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/t1/tbl1/en/tv.action?pid=1410028701\",\"series_title\":\"Canada;Unemployment rate;Total - Gender;15 years and over;Estimate;Seasonally adjusted\",\"unit\":\"Percent\",\"scale\":\"units\",\"frequency\":\"Monthly\",\"geography\":\"Canada\",\"members\":[{\"dimension\":\"Geography\",\"member\":\"Canada\",\"member_id\":1},{\"dimension\":\"Labour force characteristics\",\"member\":\"Unemployment rate\",\"member_id\":7},{\"dimension\":\"Gender\",\"member\":\"Total - Gender\",\"member_id\":1},{\"dimension\":\"Age group\",\"member\":\"15 years and over\",\"member_id\":1},{\"dimension\":\"Statistics\",\"member\":\"Estimate\",\"member_id\":1},{\"dimension\":\"Data type\",\"member\":\"Seasonally adjusted\",\"member_id\":1}],\"table_release_time\":\"2026-11-06T08:30\",\"first_period\":\"1976-01-01\",\"last_period\":\"2026-10-01\",\"notes\":[]},\"observations\":[{\"ref_period\":\"2026-08-01\",\"value\":6.4,\"decimals\":1,\"scalar_factor_code\":0,\"scale_multiplier\":1,\"symbol_code\":0,\"status_code\":0,\"security_level_code\":0,\"release_time\":\"2026-11-06T13:30:00Z\",\"symbol\":\"none\",\"status\":\"normal\",\"security_level\":\"public\"},{\"ref_period\":\"2026-09-01\",\"value\":6.5,\"decimals\":1,\"scalar_factor_code\":0,\"scale_multiplier\":1,\"symbol_code\":0,\"status_code\":0,\"security_level_code\":0,\"release_time\":\"2026-11-06T13:30:00Z\",\"symbol\":\"none\",\"status\":\"normal\",\"security_level\":\"public\"},{\"ref_period\":\"2026-10-01\",\"value\":6.7,\"decimals\":1,\"scalar_factor_code\":0,\"scale_multiplier\":1,\"symbol_code\":0,\"status_code\":0,\"security_level_code\":0,\"release_time\":\"2026-11-06T13:30:00Z\",\"symbol\":\"none\",\"status\":\"normal\",\"security_level\":\"public\"}],\"transformed\":null}],\"failed\":[],\"provenance\":{\"source\":\"statcan-wds\",\"url\":\"https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/t1/wds/rest/getDataFromVectorsAndLatestNPeriods\",\"queried_at\":\"2026-11-07T21:47:15.869190Z\",\"as_of\":null,\"freshness\":null,\"coverage\":null,\"limits\":null,\"cached\":true,\"lang\":\"en\",\"schema_name\":\"statcan.wds.VectorDataSet\",\"licence\":\"Statistics Canada Open Licence (https://www.statcan.gc.ca/en/reference/licence). Attribution: 'Source: Statistics Canada.'\",\"commercial_use\":\"allowed\",\"caveats\":[\"LFS and SEPH employment are different measures: do not compare their levels. The LFS is a household survey that counts employed people (a person with two jobs counts once), including the self-employed and agriculture; SEPH counts payroll jobs, so it leaves out the self-employed and agriculture, fishing and trapping, private household services, religious organisations and military personnel of the defence services. LFS estimates carry sampling error; preliminary SEPH estimates are revised. Compare trends over several months, not one month's change. For earnings in a detailed industry, such as provincial and territorial public administration (NAICS 912), use SEPH (14-10-0203 monthly, 14-10-0204 annual) and say why: the LFS wage table 14-10-0064 stops at broad sectors ('Public administration' as a whole).\",\"LFS figures are survey estimates. Table 14-10-0287 publishes the standard error of each estimate, of its month-to-month change and of its year-over-year change (the Statistics dimension). A change is significant at the 5% level only when the change plus or minus two standard errors excludes zero, which many small monthly moves do not. Statistics Canada releases estimates with a CV up to 16.5% freely, with a warning up to 33.3%, and not above; estimates under a minimum size (1,500 for Canada) are suppressed. Seasonally adjusted series are revised once a year.\"],\"reproduce\":\"For scripts, call reproduce_code with this tool's name and arguments.\"}}","type":"text"}],"isError":false,"structuredContent":{"series":[{"product_id":14100287,"coordinate":"1.7.1.1.1.1.0.0.0.0","vector_id":2062815,"context":{"citation":"Statistics Canada. Table 14-10-0287-01, Labour force characteristics, monthly, seasonally adjusted and trend-cycle. Vector v2062815. Released 2026-11-06.","table_id":"14-10-0287-01","table_title":"Labour force characteristics, monthly, seasonally adjusted and trend-cycle","table_url":"https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/t1/tbl1/en/tv.action?pid=1410028701","series_title":"Canada;Unemployment rate;Total - Gender;15 years and over;Estimate;Seasonally adjusted","unit":"Percent","scale":"units","frequency":"Monthly","geography":"Canada","members":[{"dimension":"Geography","member":"Canada","member_id":1},{"dimension":"Labour force characteristics","member":"Unemployment rate","member_id":7},{"dimension":"Gender","member":"Total - Gender","member_id":1},{"dimension":"Age group","member":"15 years and over","member_id":1},{"dimension":"Statistics","member":"Estimate","member_id":1},{"dimension":"Data type","member":"Seasonally adjusted","member_id":1}],"table_release_time":"2026-11-06T08:30","first_period":"1976-01-01","last_period":"2026-10-01","notes":[]},"observations":[{"ref_period":"2026-08-01","value":6.4,"decimals":1,"scalar_factor_code":0,"scale_multiplier":1,"symbol_code":0,"status_code":0,"security_level_code":0,"release_time":"2026-11-06T13:30:00Z","symbol":"none","status":"normal","security_level":"public"},{"ref_period":"2026-09-01","value":6.5,"decimals":1,"scalar_factor_code":0,"scale_multiplier":1,"symbol_code":0,"status_code":0,"security_level_code":0,"release_time":"2026-11-06T13:30:00Z","symbol":"none","status":"normal","security_level":"public"},{"ref_period":"2026-10-01","value":6.7,"decimals":1,"scalar_factor_code":0,"scale_multiplier":1,"symbol_code":0,"status_code":0,"security_level_code":0,"release_time":"2026-11-06T13:30:00Z","symbol":"none","status":"normal","security_level":"public"}],"transformed":null}],"failed":[],"provenance":{"source":"statcan-wds","url":"https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/t1/wds/rest/getDataFromVectorsAndLatestNPeriods","queried_at":"2026-11-07T21:47:15.869190Z","as_of":null,"freshness":null,"coverage":null,"limits":null,"cached":true,"lang":"en","schema_name":"statcan.wds.VectorDataSet","licence":"Statistics Canada Open Licence (https://www.statcan.gc.ca/en/reference/licence). Attribution: 'Source: Statistics Canada.'","commercial_use":"allowed","caveats":["LFS and SEPH employment are different measures: do not compare their levels. The LFS is a household survey that counts employed people (a person with two jobs counts once), including the self-employed and agriculture; SEPH counts payroll jobs, so it leaves out the self-employed and agriculture, fishing and trapping, private household services, religious organisations and military personnel of the defence services. LFS estimates carry sampling error; preliminary SEPH estimates are revised. Compare trends over several months, not one month's change. For earnings in a detailed industry, such as provincial and territorial public administration (NAICS 912), use SEPH (14-10-0203 monthly, 14-10-0204 annual) and say why: the LFS wage table 14-10-0064 stops at broad sectors ('Public administration' as a whole).","LFS figures are survey estimates. Table 14-10-0287 publishes the standard error of each estimate, of its month-to-month change and of its year-over-year change (the Statistics dimension). A change is significant at the 5% level only when the change plus or minus two standard errors excludes zero, which many small monthly moves do not. Statistics Canada releases estimates with a CV up to 16.5% freely, with a warning up to 33.3%, and not above; estimates under a minimum size (1,500 for Canada) are suppressed. Seasonally adjusted series are revised once a year."],"reproduce":"For scripts, call reproduce_code with this tool's name and arguments."}}}}

